-- Q12119: Inventory [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Debit Inventory $16,000 and credit Sales Revenue $16,000","Debit Cost of Goods Sold $16,000 and credit Inventory $16,000","Debit Other Comprehensive Income $16,000 and credit Inventory $16,000","No entry is required because FIFO inventory remains at historical cost"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 330-10-35 (amended by ASU 2015-11), FIFO inventory must be written down when NRV falls below cost. The $16,000 write-down ($125,000 − $109,000) is charged to COGS or a loss account with a credit to Inventory.
Wrong (A): Inventory write-downs are not credited to Sales Revenue; the loss flows through cost of goods sold or a separate loss line.
Wrong (C): Inventory impairments are recognized in net income, not in other comprehensive income.
Wrong (D): ASU 2015-11 requires FIFO inventory to be measured at the lower of cost and NRV, not held at historical cost.$EXPL$
