-- Q12164: Payables and Accrued Liabilities [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["An amount withheld from progress billings until project completion or contract satisfaction","A penalty assessed against the contractor for late delivery of project materials","An advance payment made by the owner to secure the contractor''s availability","A surety bond posted by the general contractor to guarantee project performance"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 606-10-45-3 and construction industry practice, retention (retainage) payable represents amounts withheld from contractor billings — typically 5% to 10% — until specified milestones or substantial completion. The withheld amount is a liability of the entity.
Wrong (B): Retention is not a penalty; it is a contractual withholding mechanism to ensure satisfactory completion.
Wrong (C): Advance payments are prepayments made before work begins, not amounts withheld from earned billings.
Wrong (D): A performance bond is a surety instrument, not a billing withholding arrangement between owner and contractor.$EXPL$
