-- Q12274: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Revenue must be disaggregated solely by product line categories","Disaggregation is optional but encouraged for all public reporting companies","Revenue must be disaggregated into categories depicting how economic factors affect its nature and timing","Revenue must be disaggregated solely by geographic region of operations"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 606-10-50-5, entities must disaggregate recognized revenue into categories that depict how the nature, amount, timing, and uncertainty of revenue and cash flows are affected by economic factors. Common categories include type, geography, and timing of transfer.
Wrong (A): Product line is one possible category, but the standard does not restrict disaggregation to that single dimension.
