-- Q12296: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Net, because NetMarket does not obtain control of the goods before customer transfer","Gross, because NetMarket processes customer payments and facilitates the full transaction","Gross, because NetMarket bears credit risk on the customer payment amounts collected","Net, because the commission rate charged to sellers is below the 20% threshold"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 606-10-55-36 through 55-40, the principal versus agent determination depends on whether the entity controls the good before transfer. Since NetMarket does not take title or bear inventory risk, it acts as an agent and recognizes only its 15% commission as revenue.
